---
/**
 * Ticket terms.
 *
 * Drafted as placeholder commercial wording that reflects how the system
 * actually behaves - reservations, QR admission, refund routes - so that the
 * operators and their solicitor are editing something concrete rather than
 * starting from a blank page. It is NOT legal advice and must be reviewed
 * before launch (AMPED-11).
 */
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/site/PageHeader.astro';
import Callout from '@/components/ui/Callout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site.ts';

export const prerender = true;
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Ticket terms"
  description="Ticket terms and conditions for Amped Up Music Promotions: refunds, cancellations, postponements and admission."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="The small print"
    title="Ticket terms"
    intro="What you are buying, what happens if a gig changes, and how you get in."
    trail={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }]}
    wide={false}
  />

  <div class="container terms">
    <Callout tone="warn" label="Draft" title="Placeholder wording">
      <p>
        These terms are a working draft written to match how the ticketing actually behaves. They
        must be reviewed before the site takes real money.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>1. Who you are buying from</h2>
      <p>
        Tickets are sold by {SITE.name}, the promoter of the event, not by the venue and not by a
        ticketing agency. Any question about your order comes to us:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.ticketsEmail}`}>{SITE.ticketsEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Prices and fees</h2>
      <p>
        The price shown on the event page is the total price. We do not add booking fees, service
        charges or payment fees at checkout. Prices include VAT where it applies.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Buying a ticket</h2>
      <p>
        When you start a checkout we hold your tickets for a short period (currently 30 minutes)
        while you pay. If the payment is not completed in that window the hold is released and the
        tickets go back on sale.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your order is only confirmed once we have independently verified the payment with our
        payment provider. A message in your browser saying the payment succeeded is not on its own
        confirmation; the confirmation email is.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Your tickets</h2>
      <p>
        Tickets are emailed to you, each with its own QR code. The QR code is an admission
        credential and contains no personal information. Each ticket admits one person once.
      </p>
      <p>
        If the email does not arrive, check your spam folder and then contact us. You do not need
        the email to get in: we can find your order on the door by name, email address, order
        reference or ticket reference.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Admission</h2>
      <p>
        Age restrictions are shown on every event page and are set by the venue licence. Where a
        show is 18+, photo ID is required. The venue may refuse admission in line with its own
        conditions of entry, including for intoxication or behaviour.
      </p>
      <p>
        Doors and stage times are our best information at the time of publishing and can change.
      </p>

      <h2>6. If we cancel</h2>
      <p>
        If we cancel an event you are entitled to a full refund of the ticket price. We will email
        everyone who holds a ticket and refund automatically to the card used. Refunds normally
        appear within five working days.
      </p>

      <h2>7. If we postpone or move the venue</h2>
      <p>
        If an event is postponed your ticket remains valid for the rescheduled date. If the new date
        does not suit you, tell us and we will refund you in full - you do not have to give a
        reason. If we change the venue we will tell you and the same choice applies.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Change of line-up</h2>
      <p>
        Support acts occasionally change. A change to a support act is not grounds for a refund. If
        the headline act does not appear, the event is treated as cancelled.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Refunds and resale</h2>
      <p>
        Tickets are non-refundable except in the circumstances above. You may transfer a ticket to
        someone else - just send them the ticket email - but tickets may not be resold for more than
        the face value. We reserve the right to void tickets we believe have been resold at a
        profit.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your data</h2>
      <p>
        We store your name, email address and order details so that we can sell you a ticket and let
        you in. We never store card details. See our <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Access</h2>
      <p>
        Accessible viewing positions and free personal assistant tickets are available at the venues
        that can offer them. See our <a href="/accessibility">accessibility information</a> and
        contact us after booking.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by
        negligence, or for fraud. Your statutory rights are not affected.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name}, <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .terms {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    padding-bottom: var(--s-9);
  }
</style>
